bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    ws_accept_hash_sha1_bytes_reencoded_utf8_before_base64_2026_11_10, 0, "compute_websocket_accept (src/lib/nogc_sync_mut/websocket/handshake.spl) and compute_accept_value (src/lib/nogc_async_mut/websocket/upgrade.spl) routed the 20 raw SHA-1 digest bytes through text (ws_bytes_to_text/char_from_code) before base64, so every byte >= 0x80 was UTF-8 re-encoded as two bytes: RFC 6455 key dGhlIHNhbXBsZSBub25jZQ== produced wrN6TyzDgGJPFsKQw7ZGBsOPOFlFwrLCvsOEw6o= instead of s3pPLMBiTxaQ9kYGzzhZRbK+xOo=. test/01_unit/app/ui/ws_handler_spec.spl was 12/14."

bugs_active |id, severity, status, title, file, line, reproducible_by, created_at, updated_at, valid|
    ws_accept_hash_sha1_bytes_reencoded_utf8_before_base64_2026_11_10, P2, fix-implemented-verification-pending, "Sec-WebSocket-Accept base64s UTF-8 re-encoded SHA-1 digest instead of raw bytes", src/lib/nogc_sync_mut/websocket/handshake.spl, 269, test/01_unit/lib/nogc_sync_mut/websocket/ws_accept_raw_digest_base64_spec.spl, 2026-11-10, 2026-11-10, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    ws_accept_hash_sha1_bytes_reencoded_utf8_before_base64_2026_11_10, 0, "2026-11-10 fix: added base64_encode_bytes(List<i64>) and used it on the raw digest in compute_websocket_accept (base64_encode now wraps it); async compute_accept_value delegates to compute_websocket_accept. Other GUID sites (http/ws/ws_handshake.spl, browser_engine ws_crypto.spl) were already raw-byte. Spec test/01_unit/lib/nogc_sync_mut/websocket/ws_accept_raw_digest_base64_spec.spl red 1/5 -> green 5/5 (RFC 6455 section 1.3 example, both owners). ws_handler_spec second failure was a stale duplicate example (expects query token from _extract_bearer) contradicting the in-file security example for the same path (query tokens rejected unless compat; env never enables it); deleted it. ws_handler_spec 12/14 -> 13/13."
    ws_accept_hash_sha1_bytes_reencoded_utf8_before_base64_2026_11_10, 1, "2026-11-11 audit: ws_crypto.compute_accept_key (gc_async_mut browser_engine) and ws_handshake.ws_compute_accept_key (nogc_sync_mut http/ws) both base64 raw digest [i64] bytes already; no fix needed. Pinned by test/01_unit/lib/nogc_sync_mut/websocket/ws_accept_other_owners_spec.spl 2/2 green on the RFC 6455 example. Not consolidated into one owner: different layers, separate byte-encoders; routing would be a cross-family import."
